(MORROW ACQUIRING | OPERATING NOTE M-4 | 2026-08-01) Tj
T*
(Fictional merchant settlement rules. Currency: CNY. A settlement batch and a dispute case) Tj
T*
(have different identifiers. A case reference is not a payout instruction. This note governs) Tj
T*
(reserve movements, not cardholder credit limits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(BATCH CLOCK) Tj
T*
(Transactions accepted before 18:00 enter that business day's batch; exactly 18:00 enters) Tj
T*
(the next business day's batch. Settlement is on T+2 business days. Saturdays, Sundays and) Tj
T*
(the published closed days are skipped. The examples below assume no closed days other than) Tj
T*
(weekends.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(RESERVE MATRIX) Tj
T*
(Standard merchant: withhold 6% of gross accepted sales.) Tj
T*
(Elevated merchant: withhold 12% of gross accepted sales.) Tj
T*
(A merchant with both flags uses Elevated only, not 18%. Refunds do not reduce the reserve) Tj
T*
(base of the batch in which they are paid. Transaction fees are separate deductions and do) Tj
T*
(not reduce the reserve base either.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(LEDGER DISCIPLINE) Tj
T*
(Operations reconcile accepted sale IDs to the terminal report before sending the batch for) Tj
T*
(review. A void made before acceptance never becomes a gross sale. A refund made after) Tj
T*
(acceptance is a separate debit, even when its amount equals the original sale. Reviewers) Tj
T*
(may attach card scheme messages as context; those messages cannot replace a matched sale) Tj
T*
(ID. A manual note does not change an accepted timestamp. Archived batch reports retain the) Tj
T*
(original risk flag to explain historical reserves.) Tj
T*
() Tj
