(WORKED BATCH) Tj
T*
(A Standard merchant has gross accepted sales of 50,000, refunds of 8,000, transaction fees) Tj
T*
(of 500 and a matured old reserve release of 1,000. No other debit applies. Payout equals) Tj
T*
(gross sales minus refunds, fees and the new reserve, plus the matured release. An unrelated) Tj
T*
(open dispute has no deduction until a provisional debit is posted.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(DISPUTE PATH) Tj
T*
(A provisional dispute debit is posted when a case is opened with a scheme debit notice. The) Tj
T*
(merchant has 7 calendar days after notice to submit a matched receipt and delivery proof. A) Tj
T*
(response with only a receipt is incomplete. Winning a case reverses the provisional debit;) Tj
T*
(it does not create another sale or reduce a reserve that was correctly withheld.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(RESERVE RELEASE) Tj
T*
(Each reserve lot matures 90 calendar days after its batch date. Release requires maturity) Tj
T*
(and no open dispute linked to that lot. An unlinked dispute does not block that lot. Lots) Tj
T*
(are tracked separately: one blocked lot cannot justify retaining every other mature lot. No) Tj
T*
(interest is paid on held reserves under M-4.) Tj
T*
() Tj
